The memory predates the Bun -> Node and OpenTUI -> Clack migrations and
had rotted. Verified against the code on 2026-09-25, these claims were
false:

- 'fixed in commit aeac85b' - no such object in the repository
- 'launcher ignores SIGINT around its spawnSync' - bin/aicmd.js imports
  dist/ or the TS entry directly; there is no spawnSync
- 'askLine resolves null on readline EOF/Ctrl-C' - askLine is gone
  (Clack prompts)
- 'engines node >=22.12' - now ^24.21.0
- 'exports map exposes index.ts under the bun condition only' - exports
  is only ./package.json
- 'OpenTUI picker mouse-click can double-move' - OpenTUI is gone
- 'user should git commit --amend -S --no-edit if still HEAD' - a stale
  imperative about a commit that no longer exists

Agents load this memory as context, so stale facts steer them wrong.
The rewrite keeps the still-true hardening list (command hygiene, guard
patterns, argument parsing, SIGINT) and points at AGENTS.md for the
safety-routing invariants instead of restating them.
---
 .../memories/adversarial-review-2026-08-18.md | 50 ++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.serena/memories/adversarial-review-2026-08-18.md b/.serena/memories/adversarial-review-2026-08-18.md
index 96a9022..e719e22 100644
--- a/.serena/memories/adversarial-review-2026-08-18.md
+++ b/.serena/memories/adversarial-review-2026-08-18.md
@@ -1,32 +1,22 @@
-# Adversarial review outcome (2026-08-18)
+# Hardening from the 2026-08-18 adversarial review
 
-A 17-agent workflow (5 lens reviewers + adversarial verifiers) reviewed the
-initial aicmd implementation. 8 confirmed findings + credible cap-dropped ones
-were all fixed in commit `aeac85b`. Key hardening that future changes must not
-regress:
+A multi-agent review of the first implementation produced these properties.
+Each is pinned by tests; keep them when refactoring.
 
-- **Danger-signal provenance**: `GeneratedCommand.modelAssessed` /
-  `DangerAssessment.modelSignalAvailable`. The plain-text fallback can't carry
-  the model's danger verdict, so `-x` refuses unassessed commands without
-  `-f` (`decideAction` in src/cli.ts — table-tested; a fail-open mutation
-  here previously survived the whole suite).
-- **`normaliseCommand`** (src/prompts.ts) rejects control chars / newlines on
-  BOTH paths — display-vs-execution spoofing via `\r`/ESC.
-- **Guard regexes**: rm rule covers `/bin/rm`, `sudo /bin/rm`, `\rm`;
-  curl|sh matches multi-stage pipes; added find -delete, rsync --delete,
-  truncate -s 0, crontab -r. Patterns carry human labels
-  (DEFAULT_PATTERN_TABLE).
-- **Commander**: `enablePositionalOptions().passThroughOptions()` — options
-  only before the first task word ("quoting optional" promise).
-- **SIGINT**: executeCommand detaches ALL process SIGINT listeners while the
-  child runs (cli's two-stage force-quit would otherwise orphan it);
-  launcher ignores SIGINT around its spawnSync; `askLine` resolves null on
-  readline EOF/Ctrl-C (previously hung).
-- **Packaging**: engines node >=22.12 (commander 15 floor), prepack builds
-  dist, exports map exposes index.ts under the `bun` condition only, os
-  darwin/linux, tsconfig `erasableSyntaxOnly`.
-
-Known accepted gaps: OpenTUI picker mouse-click can double-move (no public
-`focusable` option; cosmetic). Final fix commit was unsigned (1Password
-locked mid-session) — user should `git commit --amend -S --no-edit` if still
-HEAD.
+- **Command hygiene**: `normaliseCommand` (src/prompts.ts) rejects control
+  characters and newlines on every candidate, so the confirmed text is always
+  the executed text (no `\r`/ESC display spoofing).
+- **Guard patterns** (`DEFAULT_PATTERN_TABLE` in src/safety.ts, each with a
+  human label): `rm` as a command token including `/bin/rm`, `sudo /bin/rm`
+  and `\rm`; `curl|sh` through multi-stage pipes; `find -delete`,
+  `rsync --delete`, `truncate -s 0`, `crontab -r`.
+- **Argument parsing**: Commander `enablePositionalOptions().passThroughOptions()`
+  (src/cli.ts) - options only before the first task word, so quoting the task
+  stays optional.
+- **SIGINT**: `executeCommand` (src/exec.ts) detaches every process SIGINT
+  listener while the child runs, so the CLI's two-stage force-quit cannot
+  orphan it.
+- **Safety routing**: the invariants live in AGENTS.md ("Safety behavior is
+  load-bearing"). `decideAction` (src/cli.ts) is a pure function with a
+  table test; keep that table exhaustive, because a fail-open mutation there
+  is invisible to every other test.
